87001-c26adb37-30d3-44cf-ad21-b458690c7d7f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b8034ffa8e39fb41c23d257ff18b9a648c573984fc513b33f46faea804a05ae9","event_uuid":"cab18d6b-7574-4b90-8633-9c91da18c569","position":{"commit_sha":"9895c1950220eba552ddacb798e0bc64c8fe3ef6","position":"1788859467584545001-cab18d6b-7574-4b90-8633-9c91da18c569"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aacd52ca653d8a4b8ef994501bab15c17966bfbc181ca671982c8172aeb3d185","event_uuid":"51cf1fc5-5312-41ff-a418-d643d465fe38","position":{"commit_sha":"c2ab26870f08b798bdf07e8fb5b0654ab9feb865","position":"1788859473207402001-51cf1fc5-5312-41ff-a418-d643d465fe38"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: Verified-0 voting REJECTED (limbo without auto-rerun); CI concurrency groups REJECTED (serializes a dozen in-flight changes). Approved direction: step-level retry of transport faults INSIDE the CI job + explicit infrastructure fault, not your change message on retry exhaustion.","timestamp":1788761541381446001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and merged as Gerrit change 2827. RCA: the triage script only rendered timeout/cancelled/failed, so a checkout transport fault that exhausted the in-job retries would still read like a code/test failure. The fix adds portable observable transport markers (git RPC HTTP 5xx, fatal unable to access, TLS/connectivity/timeouts, hung-up/early EOF) and reports INFRASTRUCTURE/TRANSPORT FAULT with wording that CI could not obtain the source and is not judging the change. Genuine pytest/test failures remain FAILED. RED was tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py showing a captured Gerrit checkout 504/RPC annotation classified as FAILED; GREEN targeted tests passed; full make verify passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset; Gerrit 2827 passed LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 and was submitted.","timestamp":1788859001057410001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788657196395863384,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f116bb54-277b-451f-b747-96f6c609cfb8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1"},{"link_uuid":"56d1b236-445c-4683-b50b-127e8a2c41c1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7263-66d7-8ade-47c4"},{"link_uuid":"51cf1fc5-5312-41ff-a418-d643d465fe38","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"be9d-2f2d-47ca-45d2"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe Gerrit Verified route used to collapse Gerrit checkout transport faults into ordinary CI failures. A checkout 504/RPC failure happens before patchset code runs, so it is not evidence that the change is broken. Operator ruling recorded 2026-09-06/07 rejected Verified-0-on-fault and CI concurrency groups; the approved direction is in-job step-level retry for transport operations plus an explicit infrastructure-fault message if retries exhaust.\n\n## RCA\n\nThe old path had two weaknesses:\n\n1. Gerrit patchset checkout steps were single-attempt operations, so transient 5xx/TLS/RPC/dispatch faults could terminate a Verified route before code executed.\n2. `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py` only distinguished timeout/cancelled/failed. If an exhausted checkout transport fault still made the run fail, the triage comment said `FAILED`, which implied a code/test verdict even though the failure was infrastructure.\n\nThe retry half landed in ticket `ergophobic-harassed-peacock` / Gerrit change 2823. This ticket finishes the signal-quality half by teaching the summary classifier to call checkout transport faults infrastructure faults, while preserving genuine test failures as `FAILED`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A captured Gerrit checkout HTTP 504/RPC failure is classified distinctly from a test failure as an infrastructure/transport fault.\n- [x] The transport-fault wording says CI could not obtain the source and that this is not a statement about the change.\n- [x] A genuine test failure still classifies as `FAILED`, so real code failures still drive the normal negative verdict path.\n- [x] The transport-fault class is visible in the run summary and distinguishable at a glance.\n- [x] Detection is portable: it keys on observable git/HTTP/TLS transport error text and the checkout job/action context, not on provider-private APIs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- RED: `pytest tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py -q` failed before the classifier change because a captured Gerrit checkout 504/RPC annotation rendered as `FAILED`.\n- GREEN: `pytest tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py -q` passed.\n- FULL: `make verify` passed with GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n- Gerrit: change 2827 merged with LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py","reason":"classify Gerrit checkout transport faults distinctly from test failures"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py","reason":"cover captured 504/RPC checkout fault and genuine failure behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7263-66d7-8ade-47c4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c26adb37-30d3-44cf-ad21-b458690c7d7f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7c9b-3afe-5a6f-4254","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI votes Verified -1 on transport failures, mislabelling infrastructure faults as broken changes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ec8d04f0-9c99-4ca6-8fe6-e03d59b17bc7","606a01a2-3d9b-434a-b3dc-18b93d95f0ab","9375dcf7-3930-4f27-9364-eaae7473e88d","e96bd998-5d21-49d7-8fad-abd9816bff7d","81222227-62de-4c63-bddf-4b84d541b922","430beeea-ea86-46c7-a7bc-c2a3e83aec13","56d1b236-445c-4683-b50b-127e8a2c41c1","36b1bc47-8df4-407f-bd4a-9bb1facae3fc","f0d08c6b-9802-4733-bc05-82bf4495b190","c26adb37-30d3-44cf-ad21-b458690c7d7f","cab18d6b-7574-4b90-8633-9c91da18c569","51cf1fc5-5312-41ff-a418-d643d465fe38"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788870024535340266,"uuid":"77fa40c6-5cda-4143-a96c-84315c04c56a"}